# Byte offsets in diagnostics, snapshots, and golden files depend on exact
# line endings. Without this, Git on Windows (core.autocrlf=true) checks these
# files out with CRLF, every offset after the first line shifts, and tests that
# pass on one machine fail on another. Pin them to LF everywhere.
*.plat       text eol=lf
*.diag.json  text eol=lf
*.stdout     text eol=lf
*.snap       text eol=lf
*.rs         text eol=lf
*.md         text eol=lf
*.toml       text eol=lf
